{
  "dom_id": "step-q346457",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The following table shows the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[10,16].$\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $12$ | $13.5$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $7$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum, with the three subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area $A$ under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[10,16].$ \n\n$A\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA\u2248f(12)\u0394{x}_{1}+f(13.5)\u0394{x}_{2}+f(16)\u0394{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $\u0394{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\u0394{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $\u0394x$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $12$ | $13.5$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\u0394x$ | $-$ | $2$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u22482\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1.5+3\\cdot 2.5 \\\\  & =4+6+7.5 \\\\  & =17.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
